## Applicable domain decisions

Retain only relevant items; fill their actual semantics.

- Units, currencies, precision, rounding stage/mode, and tolerances.
- Missing/invalid values, overflow, tick sizes, and lot sizes.
- Event and receipt times, exchange dates/calendars, timezones, and ordering.
- Late, duplicate, corrected, or missing events.
- Raw/adjusted market data, corporate actions, revisions, and lineage.
- Authority by field and as-of time; reconciliation exception handling.
- Account/instrument/fill identity; partial fills and durable deduplication.
- Position and P&L conventions, FX, fees, commissions, and borrow costs.
- Simulation/paper/live separation and point-in-time research data.
- Order transitions, unknown outcomes, retries, disconnects, and recovery.
- Risk enforcement with stale state and concurrent submissions.
- Audit records for consequential decisions and effects.

